---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Privacy | MathMyRate" description="What MathMyRate collects, stores, and sends: the complete list.">
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-24">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-5xl font-bold leading-none md:text-6xl">Your numbers stay yours.</h1>
    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/70">
      <p>This page describes everything MathMyRate does with data. If we ever change this, this page changes first, not a policy blog post.</p>
      <div>
        <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold text-ink">What is collected</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Nothing. There is no analytics, no tracking, no cookies, no telemetry, and no advertising on this site.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold text-ink">What is stored on your device</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">One thing: when you transfer an hourly rate into the project calculator, the rate is kept in your browser's localStorage under the key <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-base">mathmyrate:hourly-cents</code> so the other page can read it. It never leaves your browser, and clearing your site data removes it. No other inputs, income targets, expenses, sale amounts, are stored or transmitted anywhere.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold text-ink">What leaves your browser</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Calculator inputs and results are processed locally in your browser and are never sent to a server, embedded in URLs, or written to logs. Standard web hosting may generate ordinary server logs (such as IP addresses and requested URLs) operated by the hosting provider; those logs contain no financial inputs from this site's calculators.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Questions about this page can go to the site operator through the repository's issue tracker.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
